{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVkDimM1Frq6PPUjjSxj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to be notified on their phone when a staging migration finishes or fails. They want to know their options and which one I'd recommend.\n\nLet me think about the notification options available:\n\n1. **PushNotification tool** - This is available in the deferred tools, so I should check if I can use this to send a notification to their phone\n2. **SendMessage tool** - Could send a message (Slack, email, etc.) but that's less reliable for an alert\n3. **p9 skill** - The \"productive-wait\" skill mentioned in the system reminder seems relevant - it's designed for watching external operations (like deploys) and has notification channels built in\n4. **Monitoring** - The Monitor tool might help watch the process\n\nGiven the context, I think the best approach is:\n- Use the **p9 skill** which is designed specifically for this use case - watching a long-running operation and notifying when it's done\n- The p9 skill mentions \"pushes through the configured notify channels\" which would handle phone notifications\n\nHowever, I should also check if there's a simpler direct approach using PushNotification.\n\nLet me think about what makes sense:\n\n1. **p9 skill** - \"Convert any blocking external operation ... into work on the next priority. The reference implementation is a PR CI watcher... Every watcher and wait upholds the termination invariant (BRO-1701): on success, failure, OR kill it reports state + next action and pushes through the configured notify channels\"\n\nThis seems perfect for their use case. They'd use `p9 wait-for <name> --cmd '<predicate>'` to watch the migration and it will notify them.\n\n2. **PushNotification tool** - I should fetch the schema to see if I can use this directly\n\n3. **SendMessage to Slack** - Could set up a Slack notification\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The user wants this *right now* for an already-running migration. So the options are:\n- **p9 wait-for** with a command to check migration status, which will push notifications when complete\n- **Direct PushNotification** if I can access that tool's schema\n- **Custom polling script** that checks status and triggers alerts\n- **Slack or email integration** for notifications\n\nSince they mentioned not wanting to keep checking a terminal, they need something proactive. The p9 skill seems purpose-built for exactly this scenario—watching external operations and notifying through configured channels when they finish.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6941,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6941},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"593d88cb-37a8-45bd-ad7b-a85d31ebc509","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:50:04.551Z","request_id":"req_011CdVkDhmZhmbyhVr9tMLce"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVkDimM1Frq6PPUjjSxj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You've got a few solid options here:\n\n1. **p9 skill** (my pick) — This is purpose-built for exactly this: `p9 wait-for staging-migration --cmd '<your-check-command>'` watches your migration in the background and sends a notification (push, Slack, email—depends on your config) when it finishes or fails. It handles the polling so your terminal stays free, and you get notified reliably.\n\n2. **PushNotification tool** — Direct phone notification. I can trigger this, but you'd need to either check back once to restart it if it crashes, or run it in a loop. More of a one-shot than a persistent watch.\n\n3. **Slack/email** — If you're already in one of those and have it on your phone, I can set up a message to post when done.\n\n**What I'd actually set up**: The **p9 approach**. It's designed to handle the \"watch a long operation and notify\" pattern, it'll keep running even if your terminal dies, and it has a clean exit (reports the final state + next action). All you'd need to tell me is:\n\n- What's the command or check that tells you whether the migration is running/done/failed? (e.g., `curl https://staging-db/status` or `tail -f migration.log | grep \"COMPLETE\"`)\n- How do you want to be notified—push notification, Slack message, or something else?\n\nThen I can spin up the watcher for you before you head out."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6941,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6941},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"9f06605a-b3ef-4246-aba6-a81a59c144d4","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:50:08.4